:"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Tyleik Williams","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tyleik_Williams","description":"American football player (born 2003)","touched":"2026-11-23T17:51:14Z","intro":"Tyleik Williams (born February 25, 2003) is an American professional football defensive tackle for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football for the Ohio State Buckeyes, winning a national championship in 2024. Williams was selected by the Lions in the first round of the 2025 NFL draft.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Williams was born on February 25, 2003, in Manassas, Virginia, later attending Unity Reed High School. He was selected to play in the 2021 All-American Bowl. He committed to Ohio State University to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Williams played in 12 games as a true freshman at Ohio State in 2021, recording 16 tackles and five sacks. As a sophomore, he had 21 tackles and one sack. In his senior year, Williams won the 2025 College Football Playoff National Championship, as Ohio State defeated Notre Dame by a score of 34 to 23."},{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"Williams was selected by the Detroit Lions in the first round as the 28th overall pick in the 2025 NFL draft."}],"social":{}},"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4431615","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/W/WillTy02.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/tyleik-williams/145080","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/tyleik-williams/12388","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tyleik_Williams"},"insights":["Ranks 1st of 114 qualified interior defensive linemen in missed-tackle %.","Ranks 21st of 115 qualified interior defensive linemen in hurries.","On the field for 47% of Detroit’s defensive snaps this season.","2026 cap number of $3.7M is the 17th-largest on the roster.","Under contract through 2028."]}